WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.767
Matrices.

2
00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.686
Forget tables of numbers.

3
00:00:03.686 --> 00:00:08.867
A matrix is a machine that moves vectors, and every neural network layer is one.

4
00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:14.367
A matrix is a grid of numbers, but what it does matters more than how it looks.

5
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:20.100
Multiply a vector by it, and the vector gets rotated, stretched, sheared or projected.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.019
It can even change the number of dimensions.

7
00:00:23.019 --> 00:00:27.067
And the weights of a neural network layer are exactly such a matrix.

8
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.933
Here is the plain grid, with two arrows along the x axis and the y axis.

9
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.467
Now we multiply everything by a rotation matrix.

10
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:41.033
The whole grid turns forty five degrees, and every vector on it turns too.

11
00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:43.900
Now look inside the matrix.

12
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.733
The first column tells you where the x axis arrow lands: up and to the right.

13
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:52.265
The second column tells you where the y axis lands.

14
00:00:52.265 --> 00:00:55.433
Those two columns decide the whole transformation.

15
00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:58.600
Here is that rotation in NumPy.

16
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.467
We build a two by two matrix from sine and cosine of forty five degrees.

17
00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.867
Then we place a probe on the x axis.

18
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:12.419
The at sign applies the matrix, and the probe moves to zero point seven, zero point seven.

19
00:01:12.419 --> 00:01:14.433
Rotated, exactly as promised.

20
00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:17.700
Here is where it shows up in real work.

21
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.700
Your exoplanet classifier takes a planet as twelve features.

22
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.733
The first dense layer multiplies it by a twelve by sixty four weight matrix.

23
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:32.095
Out comes a sixty four dimensional version where the classes are easier to separate.

24
00:01:32.095 --> 00:01:34.867
Training just nudges the numbers in that grid.

25
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:36.894
Let's recap.

26
00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:40.133
A matrix is a transformation, not just a table.

27
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.067
Its columns show where the basis vectors land.

28
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.367
It can change the number of dimensions.

29
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.731
And neural network weights are matrices doing exactly this.

30
00:01:49.731 --> 00:01:51.867
Next up: matrix multiplication.
